<title>USA: USA Today.</title>
<headline>USA Today.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nike suspended a manager of its plant in Vietnam following a labour rights group report about worker abuse, USA Today reported Thursday.</p>
<p>Vietnam Labour Watch inspected Nike factories there and found violations of minimum wage and overtime laws, as well as physical mistreatment, the paper said. The report would be released Thursday in New York, it said.</p>
<p>The company was not immediately available to comment.</p>
</text>
